##	Notes on various possible encoding schemes to shrink the number of characters required to store YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS:
##		YYYMM:
##			- YYYYMMDD ............. 29991231 → b62  = 21q5X, 5 digits
##			- YYYYMMDD ............. 29991231 → b32c = WK89Z, 5 digits
##			- YYYYMM ............... 299912   → b62  =  1G1I, 4 digits
##			- YYYY ................. 2999     → b32c =   2XQ, 3 digits
##		*	- YYYY ................. 2999     → b62  =    mN, 2 digits until year 3843
##			- Year as 3-digits .....  999     → b32c =    Z7, 2 digits
##			- Year as 3-digits .....  999     → b62  =    G7, 2 digits
##			- YYYMM ................  99912   → b32c =  31J8, 4 digits
##			- YYYMM ................  99912   → b62  =   PzU, 3 digits
##			- Month up to max ......     12   → b32c =     C, 1 digits
##			- Month up to max ......     12   → b62  =     C, 1 digits
##			- Day up to max ........       31 → b32c =     Z, 1 digit
##			- Day up to max ........       31 → b62  =     V, 1 digit
##		HHMMSS:
##			- HHMMSS .............. 235959 → b32c = 76DQ, 4 digits
##			- HHMMSS .............. 235959 → b62  = zNn,  3 digits
##				or
##			- HH .................. 23     → b32c =    Q, 1 digit
##			- HH .................. 23     → b62  =    N, 1 digit
##			- MMSS ................   5959 → b32c  = 5T7, 3 digits
##			- MM ..................   59   → b32c  =  1V, 2 digits
##			- MM ..................   59   → b62  =    x, 1 digit
##			- SS ..................     59 → b62  =    x, 1 digit
##			= ........................................... 3 digits
##		Base32c:
##			- YYYYMMDDHHMMSS ...............: V8VGAY9VQ   9  Millenium and second accurate
##			-  YYYMMDDHHMMSS ...............: 92S1WKSVQ   9  Century and second
##			-  YYYMMDDHHMMS ................:  X2G61ZCB   8  Century and ten-second
##			- [YYYY][MM][DD][HH][MM][SS] ...:  2XQCZNQQ   8  Millenium and second, separate digits for each unit of time
##			- [ YYY][MM][DD][HH][MM][SS] ...:   Z7CZNQQ   7  Century and second, separate digits for each unit of time
##			- [ YYY][MM][DD][HHMMSS] .......:  Z7CZ76DQ   8 Century and second
##		Base62:
##			- YYYYMMDDHHMMSS ...............: 8W0lprLr    8  Millenium and second, 8 chars until year ~21,000
##			-  YYYMMDDHHMMSS ...............: 2ptsK3iZ    8  Century and second
##			-  YYYMMDDHHMMS ................:  HaaQnyF    7  Century and ten-second
##			- [YYYY][MM][DD][HH][MM][SS] ...:  mNCVNxx    7  Millenium and second, separate digits for each unit of time
##			- [ YYY][MM][DD][HH][MM][SS] ...:  G7CVNxx    7  Century and second, separate digits for each unit of time
##			- [ YYY][MM][DD][HHMMSS] .......:  G7CVzNn    7  Century and second accurate
##		Base62 [YYY*] and various evenly divided divisions:
##			- [YYY][YMMDDHHMMSS_4] .........:  G7zzzz     6  Centuryaccurate, year evenly divided into 2.134-second intervals
##			- [2YYY][MMDDHHMMSS_3] .........:   mNzzz     5  Century accurate, month evenly divided into 11.2-second intervals
##		*	- [2YYY][MM][DD][HHMMSS_2] .....:  mNCVzz     6  Century accurate, day evenly divided into 22.48-second intervals
##		Seconds since 1970 (unix time): 1694050834  $(date +%s)
##			x9convertbase1 --clipout $(date --utc +%s) 32c
##			x9convertbase1 --clipout $(date --utc -d "Jan 1 2024" +%s)
##			- Base32c ......................: 1JFJAGJ     7 digits until year 3058
##			- Base48j1 .....................:  6∮6‡[j     6
##		*	- Base62 .......................:  1qe40Y     6 digits until 3769
##			- Base64j1u ....................:  1a▴IeI     6 digits until 4147
##			- Base64j1uw ...................:  1p▴m2F     6
##			- Base128jc1 ...................:   6t△🜗N     5
##		Seconds since 2000: 747335729
##			x9convertbase1 --clipout $(( $(date +%s) - $(date -d "Jan 1 2000" +%s) )) 32c
##			x9convertbase1 --clipout $(( $(date -d "Jan 1 2500" +%s) - $(date -d "Jan 1 2000" +%s) )) 32c
##			- Base32c ......................:  P8PW1H      6 digits until 2034, 7 digits until 3059
##			- Base62 .......................:   oZkA5      5 digits until 2029, 6 digits until 3799
##		Minutes since 2000: 12455595
##			x9convertbase1 --clipout $(( ($(date -d "Jan 1 2200" +%s) - $(date -d "Jan 1 2000" +%s)) / 60 )) 32c
##			- Base32c ......................:   BW3NB      5 digits until 2063, 6 digits until 4041
##			- Base62 .......................:    qGGh      4 digits until 2028, 5 digits until 3741
